viewport: unknown zoom: 1.00 natural
ok: nodes=8 edges=4 flows=0 direction=lr theme=gruvbox
canvas: 4 diagrams on one canvas, drawn whole at 100%
diagram probe-l0 "Probe L0" at 0,7: extent=31x5 nodes=2 edges=1 routes=1
  description: System context: the machine manager is one box. The control plane and humans + mmctl call it; it drives the bare-metal providers, boots and audits the machines, keeps images and diagnostics in S3, and alerts in Slack. Nothing inside is shown yet, so L1 opens it.
diagram probe-l1 "Probe L1" at 0,19: extent=31x5 nodes=2 edges=1 routes=1
  description: L0's box opened one level: its boundary services — private gRPC, webapi, provider registry, cluster reconcile, SSH + BMC ops and the boot server — sit in the Machine manager box, while the control plane, humans, providers, machines and S3 stay outside it.
diagram probe-l1b "Probe L1B" at 0,31: extent=31x5 nodes=2 edges=1 routes=1
  description: The fleet end of the same system. Bare-metal machines run the machine-agent, which registers and heartbeats into public gRPC inside the manager's box; the River queue uploads diagnostics to S3 and webapi confirms actions in Slack, both outside. The fleet drives these outward relations.
diagram probe-l2 "Probe L2" at 0,43: extent=31x5 nodes=2 edges=1 routes=1
  description: The manager's inside: requests land on the River queue, which dispatches provision jobs, audits and diagnostic events; the janitor proposes actions back to webapi, and the queue, private gRPC, public gRPC and reconcile write into Postgres. Every node here is inside the box.
extent=96x48 cells (whole canvas)
crossings: 0 bridges, 0 touching bends
near-misses: 0 cell(s) inside the 2-cell margin of a node the route does not serve (0 on trunk buses)
passes-near-unrelated-node: 0
labels: 4/4 placed, 0 leader-ticked, 0 on route, 0 skipped, 0 ambiguous owners
